WEBVTT

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:05.690
It didn't last long,

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.280
but when my husband's condition was relatively stable,

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.490
the two of us often went hiking.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.490
Even though it was just us stomping through the muck,

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.160
he looked incredibly happy then.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:24.580
I'm sorry for suddenly bringing that up.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.690
For some reason,

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:34.180
seeing you sitting there eating with such relish really cheers me up.

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:38.720
So I have a proposal.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:43.230
Would you let me wash your back while we take a bath?

00:00:54.700 --> 00:01:01.330
I didn't care what our future together would have been like

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:07.500
as we'd have sat close enough to know the other's feelings

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:14.050
I was prepared for the time you left

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:20.890
but still I found no words to encourage you

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:27.400
After I embraced you with all I had

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:36.950
a sadness that may well have been our closeness

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:40.620
filled my heart

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:47.120
Saying goodbye was for the best

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:53.800
You gave me happiness

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:57.130
Until I meet you again one day

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.640
Until I know what you are truly like

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.180
Summer Snow Rendezvous
Until I know what you are truly like

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:06.850
I won't forget your smile
Summer Snow Rendezvous

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:07.980
I won't forget your smile

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:21.200
Princess,

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:24.030
there are a lot of things I was wondering about.

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:25.320
Ask away.

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:27.740
This is "Thumbelina", right?

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:29.120
Maybe.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:32.250
What role do I play then?

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:33.960
What role do you want to be?

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.380
I get to decide?

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:38.500
It's the same thing as saying how do you want to live your life, right?

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:42.010
But isn't this a world where we're assigned parts?

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:46.140
Well, after all, you don't appear in this tale, strictly speaking.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.760
Well, yeah, that's true...

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.180
You have to think about it and decide for yourself.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:53.140
But you came over here without even preparing for that.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:55.560
How could I have imagined all of this?

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.520
In the first place, I didn't even know it was possible to loan out my body.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:02.490
Then why did you risk your life coming here?

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.990
It was spur of the moment...

00:03:04.990 --> 00:03:06.780
Even though you don't know if you'll be able to return?

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:07.780
Huh?

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:08.740
I can't go back?

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.870
I don't like the sound of that.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:12.870
It's possible, you know?

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:15.120
What would happen in that case?

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:16.130
I dunno.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.290
Am I seriously in trouble being here?

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:19.800
I dunno...

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:21.050
What should I do?

00:03:21.050 --> 00:03:22.340
Decide on my role?

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:23.420
I dunno.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:29.010
Well, I'm basically optimistic by nature, so this doesn't bother me.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:30.390
Even though you were just worried.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:31.930
No, really.

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:35.650
It's like, if there's a start, there must be a finish.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:39.320
Every rain ends eventually.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:41.570
As long as you're alive, anyway.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:44.780
In the end, it's up to you, Manager.

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:49.030
But if you're careless, you really might get lost and not be able to go back home.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.450
Your husband is the one who's lost, remember?

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:55.210
I haven't gone astray.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.590
I just want you to look at me and smile, Manager.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:00.880
Oh?

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:06.180
So, how much should I take off?

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.300
Um...

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:09.100
Everything?

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:11.680
I don't know.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:13.470
You don't have a plan?

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:16.100
Just your back is fine, then.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:18.480
And I should get in the tub like this?

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.440
Oh, that's right...

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:21.980
I'll get all wet.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:23.190
Um...

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:26.280
Then...

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.200
You know...

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:28.410
Yes?

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:33.240
I'm surprised you can ask me to do this, knowing how I feel about you.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:34.870
Sorry.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:38.790
It is a strange request, isn't it?

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:41.590
Sorry.

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:44.380
Forget about it, put your clothes back on, and refuse me!

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:45.670
You think I can refuse?

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:48.090
I'm going in first.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:49.430
Come in after.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.430
I'm saying let's take a bath together.

00:04:57.350 --> 00:05:00.810
<i>I bet Rokka is willing.</i>

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:04.400
<i>Some part of her was unconsciously hoping that sometime, somewhere,</i>

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:07.280
<i>something like this would happen.</i>

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:11.030
<i>There's nothing especially wrong with that.</i>

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:13.910
<i>But...</i>

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:19.870
Your back's getting soft.

00:05:19.870 --> 00:05:22.080
And it's pure white.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:23.590
That tickles.

00:05:23.590 --> 00:05:27.010
You need to hurry up and get well, then start putting on muscle.

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:27.670
Yeah.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:35.220
What?

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:36.890
Huh?

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:38.390
Stop that.

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:39.350
My back's dirty.

00:05:39.770 --> 00:05:41.520
It is not.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:46.570
You smell like an animal.

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:47.230
What?

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:49.150
I love stroking your back.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:52.110
The sound of your heartbeat.

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:57.120
The sound of vulnerable life from behind.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.960
It gives me peace of mind.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:02.790
Hey...

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:03.750
Please.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:05.800
Stay still.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:08.760
<i>Rokka is</i>

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:12.050
<i>already looking at a new back.</i>

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:13.590
Hazuki.

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:16.890
I'm sorry.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:18.770
I guess

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:21.770
I'm just not ready for that yet.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:23.900
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:26.270
<i>There's nothing to do.</i>

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:28.590
<i>I understand.</i>

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:31.360
<i>If I disappear, it's simple.</i>

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:33.110
<i>But I'm not ready yet.</i>

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:36.410
<i>I want to be by your side just a little longer.</i>

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:41.750
You haven't changed one bit.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:44.670
Though you have had a change of heart.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:47.000
What do you mean?

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:50.010
If you've fallen in love, you have to admit it.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:54.470
Hazuki...

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:56.010
If this is going to happen sooner or later,

00:06:56.510 --> 00:06:57.760
<i>No matter how pitiful it is...</i>

00:06:58.600 --> 00:06:59.770
I want it to be now.

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:00.850
<i>I want it to be now.</i>

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:09.780
But if the prince doesn't come back, what are you going to do?

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:13.200
If that happens, is it game over for me?

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.030
Probably.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:16.660
You'd be okay with that tragic ending?

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:18.910
Yes, since this is the prince's world.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:24.580
I finally succeeded in taking the manager to an amusement park.

00:07:24.580 --> 00:07:26.790
I still have big plans for us.

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:28.210
You're charmingly naive, huh?

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:29.170
Exactly.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:31.170
But kind of a sucker.

00:07:31.170 --> 00:07:32.420
Sticks and stones...

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:34.930
I guess...

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:38.390
I still can't get over Shimao.

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:42.890
What's so good about the manager?

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:44.980
What's so good?

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:47.060
Why do you have such strong feelings for her?

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:49.940
What do you like about her?

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:50.770
When did you first notice her?

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:52.320
When?

00:07:55.150 --> 00:08:01.200
The first time I saw her, I thought she was a really tall middle-school boy.

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.950
Huh? A boy?

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:05.250
Well, to be honest, yes.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.040
That's rude.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:09.420
But then something happened.

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:14.050
When I looked closely, I could see a rainbow,

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:19.300
formed by chance in the spray of her water.

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:23.770
She was somehow like a kid, and I couldn't take my eyes off of her.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:27.100
Even though that was my first impression,

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:30.770
I soon learned she was older and the owner of the shop.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:35.150
When I walked by her, for some reason, I caught the scent of earth.

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:39.200
That was part of it.

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:42.620
I think maybe I was,

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:46.160
or no, I was...

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:49.790
already in love with her.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:57.550
Hazuki!

00:08:58.220 --> 00:08:58.970
Wai—

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:00.890
Hazuki?!

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:13.480
What's the next part again?

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:17.740
Does Thumbelina have a happy ending after this?

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:20.410
Kidnapped by a frog,

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:22.370
surrounded by gold beetles,

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:24.660
becoming indebted to an old lady rat,

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:29.250
but once this wing is repaired, do you meet the prince in a field of flowers?

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.670
Are there flowers blooming in the prince's brain?

00:09:33.670 --> 00:09:35.000
What's wrong with you suddenly?

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:37.590
I want to get this story finished.

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:40.800
And then I wanna go right back home.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:42.760
I'm sorry.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:44.850
Even though I'm the one wh—

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.560
Stop talking like that.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:48.060
But...

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:49.940
Do you really think you're in the wrong?

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:53.400
Well...

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:56.400
You're thinking, "Whatever happens, happens."

00:09:57.860 --> 00:09:59.990
From the beginning, it's only been a matter of time.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:04.490
Not once have you seriously refused me.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:09.410
I want you to stop using your dead husband as an excuse like this.

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:18.630
Hazuki...

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:31.140
Shimao...

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:33.690
What...

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:37.320
should I do?

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:47.160
No good.

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:50.830
Gotta take my mind off this.

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:01.090
Hmm... What shall I write?

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:02.680
Today's Pick

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:04.220
Maybe a present?
Today's Pick

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:05.140
Today's Pick

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.260
This is tough...

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.930
I'm not good at making recommendations.

00:11:10.930 --> 00:11:12.140
That's not true.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:16.650
If you assemble reasonably priced flowers by color and size,

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:21.740
you can have the customer choose which of them should be the main flowers, and then make a bouquet.

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:24.410
That isn't difficult at all, is it?

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.450
Even if you try hard to make recommendations,

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:30.370
the customer will realize you're forcing it and nothing good will come.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:32.040
I know that, but it's like...

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:34.620
Myself, I don't mind making recommendations.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.880
Just take advantage of the weather or mood of the day,

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:42.260
and use those for customers who don't know what to choose.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:43.300
Really?

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:46.340
You're too serious, Rokka.

00:11:46.340 --> 00:11:48.100
It's necessary to pay attention to their mood,

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:50.060
but there's no point in really trying to read the customer's mind.

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:53.390
If you can't decide for the customers, it's a disservice to them, Rokka.

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:59.230
<i>Why did I talk in such a roundabout way?</i>

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:04.530
I really just wanted to even out Hazuki's hair.

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:06.570
<i>Liar.</i>

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:12.330
<i>I only wanted to touch his back.</i>

00:12:13.370 --> 00:12:15.910
I have to decide what I want to do.

00:12:17.330 --> 00:12:18.830
What a mess I'm in...

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:21.000
Honestly.

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:25.470
The lights.

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:28.970
I did forget to turn them off.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:32.390
The stocker is okay.

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:34.600
The counter...

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:38.690
Oh, no. Did I forget to close it?

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.860
I've been so absent-minded lately.

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:51.580
What's this drawing?

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:56.830
<i>The princess, enshrined in settling memories...</i>

00:12:58.370 --> 00:12:59.330
<i>Potted plants,</i>

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:01.170
<i>secrets,</i>

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:03.420
<i>antiseptic...</i>

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:13.760
Sheesh! No matter how many we pull, they just keep coming up.

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:17.520
I'm sorry to drag you out here on a Sunday morning, Rokka.

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:19.020
It's nothing.

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:22.520
What do you say we take a break after finishing this corner?

00:13:22.520 --> 00:13:23.480
Good idea.

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:26.740
Damn, it's hot.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:29.320
It feels like summer.

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:31.700
Even though I meant to get this done while it was still cool outside...

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:34.080
Sorry I took up all your time with the store.

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:37.450
Oh, no, it's not that. I procrastinated because pulling weeds is a pain in the ass.

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:43.040
But if I just let 'em be, they'd take over everything.

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:44.710
Still, I'm envious of you.

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:46.960
Since you have a garden at your house.

00:13:46.960 --> 00:13:48.170
It's the size of a postage stamp.

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:49.680
It's plenty big.

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:50.970
It's a pain in the ass.

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:53.300
I wish I had one, too.

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:56.680
Come to think of it, I made beefsteak plant juice. Want some?

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:58.350
I'd love to!

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:00.350
You can't beat homemade.

00:14:00.350 --> 00:14:01.690
I can't wait!

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:04.270
I put in a little sugar and a lot of citric acid.

00:14:04.270 --> 00:14:05.480
Sounds good.

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:11.950
<i>It's finally taller than me.</i>

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:17.540
Eventually, I want to turn this into a rose arch.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:18.500
Arch?

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:19.500
Yep.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:20.910
A long one.

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:22.170
Really?

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:25.090
Like the one in <i>Alice's Adventures in Wonderland</i>.

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:26.500
There it is.

00:14:28.590 --> 00:14:29.720
There what is?

00:14:29.970 --> 00:14:32.090
You have the same interests as a young girl, Shimao.

00:14:32.470 --> 00:14:33.470
Is that bad?

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:34.600
No, nothing wrong with it.

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:37.720
I like young girls for their awkwardness.

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:39.810
"Awkwardness" is insulting.

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:41.100
It's just the image I get.

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:43.100
Even with "Life is brief. Fall in love, maidens"?

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:45.440
There's that "love me because I'm fragile" appeal.

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:47.400
I'm not trying to appeal to you.

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:48.900
I really like that poem.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:49.570
Yeah, yeah.

00:14:50.860 --> 00:14:53.780
"Life is brief. Fall in love, maidens

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:56.530
before the tides of passion cool within you,

00:14:56.530 --> 00:14:59.160
for those of you who know no tomorrow."

00:15:01.160 --> 00:15:07.960
<i>Shimao was very good at pruning and growing big roses.</i>

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:13.970
<i>The number of flowers on this branch has really increased.</i>

00:15:15.590 --> 00:15:20.600
<i>I normally love little roses like these,</i>

00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:25.560
<i>but sometimes flowers are just too eloquent.</i>

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:30.900
<i>That goes especially for a garden without a master during the summer.</i>

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.070
My back hurts...

00:15:36.070 --> 00:15:38.080
Are you busy at work?

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:41.790
I guess you could say that, but since I work from home...

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:44.920
I have to apologize for always putting you to work when you already have a profession.

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:48.500
No, working at the shop is perfect because it gives me some exercise.

00:15:48.500 --> 00:15:50.130
Well, if you put it that way...

00:15:50.710 --> 00:15:53.550
Rokka, have you been working too hard?

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:55.220
Are you able to take a breather once in a while?

00:15:56.300 --> 00:15:58.010
Well, that's kind of what today is.

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:02.180
I think you just came here to be worked hard.

00:16:02.180 --> 00:16:03.770
Don't you have anything else to do?

00:16:03.770 --> 00:16:06.230
Work is fun, too.

00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:09.060
I have no right to talk since I'm single, too,

00:16:09.060 --> 00:16:11.900
but a widow isn't meant to stay one forever.

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:13.610
Right...

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:19.830
It seems to me that you've taken on too much burden for one person.

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.030
For example,

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:23.950
you could go out with a regular customer or a young man or someone.

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:24.790
Um...

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:26.420
What's wrong all of a sudden?

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:28.040
I'd better get going.

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:31.130
The neighborhood library closes at one in the afternoon today.

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:33.340
I thought I would stop there on my way back.

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:34.340
Oh, yeah?

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:35.880
The juice was delicious.

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:36.720
Thank you!

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:37.300
Sure.

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:38.800
I'll clean up the glasses...

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:40.600
Just leave them right there.

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:42.850
Thank you. I'm really sorry for running out like this!

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:45.270
Um... Well, I'll come again soon!

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:46.520
See you later!

00:16:49.310 --> 00:16:51.060
She escaped.

00:16:53.690 --> 00:16:57.530
I feel like I'm as transparent as glass.

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:00.160
But...

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:03.290
This idea of a widow changing her status...

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:06.620
For one thing, I'd never be able to forget him.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:12.290
Maybe I can let her take care of pruning the roses.

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:16.260
The roses that Shimao grew...

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:19.510
They were ridiculously beautiful.

00:17:21.260 --> 00:17:23.680
I suppose I'm just full of regrets these days.

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:27.680
For example...

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:32.060
Assuming that I do have to move forward...

00:17:32.060 --> 00:17:36.360
I don't mind being the second choice all my life.

00:17:42.570 --> 00:17:46.330
Not once have you seriously refused me.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:51.790
I'm surprised you can ask me to do this, knowing how I feel about you.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:57.340
You're in love with me?

00:17:57.340 --> 00:17:58.840
Yes, I am!

00:17:59.590 --> 00:18:00.470
For example...

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:04.010
you could...

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:06.520
have an affair with me or something...

00:18:07.020 --> 00:18:10.770
Manager, I'm gonna live longer than you, sorry to say.

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:15.110
<i>Just telling me that at this point isn't going to make me back off.</i>

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:17.070
<i>He's always...</i>

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:18.990
If you don't look at me, I'm gonna scream.

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:20.030
<i>always...
If you don't look at me, I'm gonna scream.</i>

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:23.410
If you don't look at me, I'm gonna scream.

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:24.450
<i>always...</i>

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:27.040
How about going here on our next day off?

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:27.620
No Expiration Date
<b>Entrance Ticket</b>

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:30.040
The old newspaper subscription salesman gave them to me,

00:18:30.370 --> 00:18:31.290
so I thought we could...

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:35.250
I want you to stop using your dead husband as an excuse like this.

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:41.050
I made him turn his back on me.

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:46.810
<i>Someone younger than me said nice things.</i>

00:18:47.510 --> 00:18:48.930
<i>I got complacent.</i>

00:18:50.930 --> 00:18:53.770
<i>I was convinced that he was tough because of his youth.</i>

00:18:55.270 --> 00:18:56.480
<i>I hurt him.</i>

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:00.610
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:19:02.610 --> 00:19:03.910
I feel like a blockhead.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:05.870
Nobody says that anymore.

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.250
Hazuki...

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:15.250
U-Um...

00:19:17.250 --> 00:19:17.590
I'm s—

00:19:17.590 --> 00:19:19.420
Please be quiet in the library.

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:24.260
Sorry. That's heavy, isn't it?

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:27.970
You have enough books for a summer vacation research project.

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:31.390
Um...

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:34.100
By the way...

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:35.020
What?

00:19:35.810 --> 00:19:36.730
My...

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:43.780
My husband is the only one I...

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:48.030
He's the only one I ever...

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:55.540
My husband was my first love.

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:57.290
I think.

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:02.090
So, uh...

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:09.140
I can say that Shimao is the only person I ever really dated.

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:16.310
And I had a crush on him first.

00:20:16.310 --> 00:20:22.820
So I never thought after getting to this age that someone would have feelings for me.

00:20:23.650 --> 00:20:24.650
Rokka.

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:30.030
I never imagined...

00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:36.040
I'm sorry.

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:39.250
I...

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:42.750
I...

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:46.590
love you too, Hazuki.

00:20:47.590 --> 00:20:48.470
I love you.

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:26.300
Inside the dreams I always have

00:21:27.420 --> 00:21:32.050
you always smile

00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:36.140
Tell me why

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:40.020
it won't go away

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:41.810
I gave you everything

00:21:41.810 --> 00:21:43.650
You gave me anything

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:48.450
Forever and ever
You're everything,

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:50.110
still my everything

00:21:50.110 --> 00:21:53.320
I love you

00:21:53.320 --> 00:21:56.700
It is a miracle

00:21:56.700 --> 00:21:59.830
like fleeting snow

00:21:59.830 --> 00:22:05.800
that fell in summer

00:22:06.920 --> 00:22:12.800
If I hadn't met you

00:22:12.800 --> 00:22:16.010
I wouldn't have felt this sadness

00:22:16.010 --> 00:22:23.520
and nothing would have pressed down on my chest

00:22:23.520 --> 00:22:29.190
If I hadn't been able to meet you

00:22:29.190 --> 00:22:36.240
I would never have known the tenderness in strength

00:22:36.240 --> 00:22:41.370
When I close my eyes

00:22:41.370 --> 00:22:45.380
you're right beside me
